   <media:title>Subaru Forester/Hybrid | How-To Use DriverFocus</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/db3bNyk1Hyk?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i1.ytimg.com/vi/db3bNyk1Hyk/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>DriverFocus is your safety-minded co-pilot in the Subaru Forester. Paired with Subaru EyeSight Driver Assist Technology, it uses a camera above the multimedia display to recognize when you're distracted or drowsy. If your eyes are drooping, drifting or looking away, a chime sounds and alert messages appear. DriverFocus recognizes up to five drivers, and once you set up a user profile it can automatically recall your seat, mirror and climate settings if your vehicle is equipped with memory seats.

Applies to model years: 2026, 2027

